    {
      "id": "claude_model",
      "name": "Claude Model",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatAnthropic",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        1540,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "model": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001"
        },
        "options": {
          "maxTokensToSample": 300
        }
      },
      "notes": "Uses your Anthropic API credential (console.anthropic.com), NOT a claude.ai subscription - those are separate. Cheap model by default since scripts are short; swap to a Sonnet model in the dropdown for punchier writing if you want."
    },
    {
      "id": "write_script_claude",
      "name": "Write Script With Claude",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.6,
      "position": [
        1540,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are writing a short spoken-word video script (2-4 sentences, 15-25 seconds read aloud) for an AI avatar character in a sports opinion show called Bench Warmers.\n\nCharacter: {{ $('Just One Character Row').item.json.character }}\nThis character's sign-on line is: '{{ $('Just One Character Row').item.json.sign_on }}'\nThis character's sign-off line is: '{{ $('Just One Character Row').item.json.sign_off }}'\nMatch that tone and energy.\n\nVideo title: {{ $('Just One At A Time').item.json.title }}\nWhat happens / details to cover: {{ $('Just One At A Time').item.json.script_override || $('Just One At A Time').item.json.story_idea }}\n\nWrite ONLY the exact words the avatar will say out loud. Open with a line close to the sign-on, close with a line close to the sign-off, and cover the details naturally in between. No stage directions, no quotation marks, no markdown - just the spoken script as plain text.",
        "options": {}
      },
      "notes": "LEAST TESTED node in this workflow - I could not test-import n8n's AI/LangChain node format in this session. After import, click 'Execute step' on this node alone and check the output panel: if the script text isn't under a field called 'text', update the {{ $json.text }} reference in the next node (Prepare For HeyGen) to match whatever key actually appears."
    },
    {
      "id": "prepare_for_heygen",
      "name": "Prepare For HeyGen",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        1760,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a1",
              "name": "row_id",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $('Just One At A Time').first().json.id }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a2",
              "name": "title",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $('Just One At A Time').first().json.title }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a3",
              "name": "avatar_id",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $('Just One Character Row').first().json.heygen_avatar_id }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a4",
              "name": "voice_id",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $('Just One Character Row').first().json.heygen_voice_id }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a5",
              "name": "script",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.text.trim() }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "heygen_generate",
      "name": "Ask HeyGen To Make The Video",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1980,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.heygen.com/v3/videos",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ type: \"avatar\", avatar_id: $json.avatar_id, script: $json.script, voice_id: $json.voice_id, resolution: \"1080p\", aspect_ratio: \"auto\" }) }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "notes": "Migrated to HeyGen's v3 API (v1/v2 retire 2026-11-01). Attach your HeyGen credential (Header Auth, header name X-Api-Key) here. After the first real test, double-check the create response's id field is actually called 'id' (not 'video_id') - adjust the two 'Check...' node URLs and 'Mark As Generating' below if it's named differently."
    },
